      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Gorsuch, J., fled a concurring opinion, p. 192."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0000-0009",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Thomas, J., fled a dissenting opinion, p. 196."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 2016, when Gorgi Talevski's dementia progressed to the point that his family members could no longer care for him, they placed him in petitioner Valparaiso Care and Rehabilitation's (VCR) nursing home."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0000-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "HHC fled a petition for certiorari, which we granted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0000-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The District Court granted HHC's subsequent motion to dismiss the complaint, reasoning that no plaintiff can enforce provisions of the FNHRA via \u00a7 1983."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0000-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court of Appeals for the Seventh Circuit reversed. It concluded that, under this Court's precedent, the relevant FNHRA provisions \u201cunambiguously confer individually enforceable rights on nursing-home residents,\u201d making those rights presumptively enforceable via \u00a7 1983."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We declined to do so, reasoning that a straightforward reading of the \u201cplain language\u201d of \u00a7 1983 is required. Id., at 4."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The unnecessary-restraint and predischarge-notice provisions thus stand in stark contrast to the statutory provisions that failed Gonzaga's test in Gonzaga itself."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The unnecessary-restraint and predischarge-notice provisions use clear \u201crights-creating language,\u201d speak \u201c `in terms of the persons benefted,' \u201d and have an \u201c `unmistakable focus on the benefted class.' \u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We discern no incompatibility between the FNHRA's remedial scheme and \u00a7 1983 enforcement of the rights that the unnecessary-restraint and predischarge-notice provisions unambiguously secure."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But an actual clash\u2014one private judicial remedy against another, more expansive remedy\u2014is not required to fnd that a statute forecloses recourse to \u00a7 1983."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I agree with Justice Alito that the Federal Nursing Home Reform Act (FNHRA) cannot be enforced through Rev. Stat. \u00a7 1979, 42 U. S. C. \u00a7 1983, under Gonzaga Univ. v. Doe, 536 U. S. 273 (2002)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0005-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In sum, from the framing of the Constitution to well into\nthe 20th century, it was virtually undisputed that Congress'\nspending power was nothing more than a power to spend.\nIt included no regulatory authority to bind parties, to secure\nrights or impose duties with the force of federal law, and no\nauthority to directly regulate the States even with\ntheir consent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Perhaps the only such square holding was that of Holt v. Indiana Mfg. Co., 176 U. S. 68 (1900), which narrowly construed \u00a7 1983's predecessor statute to \u201crefer to civil rights only,\u201d making it \u201cinapplicable\u201d in a suit based on the federal patent laws."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Court \u201csimply ignored the crucial difference between restraints accepted as conditions of funding, and restraints imposed by virtue of a legislative power.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "legislation enacted pursuant to the spending power, the typical remedy for state noncompliance with federally imposed conditions is not a private cause of action for noncompliance but rather action by the Federal Government to terminate funds to the State."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0004",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "By holding that FNHRA creates rights enforceable under \u00a7 1983, the majority creates a grave constitutional problem that cannot be brushed away with a mere incantation of Thiboutot."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0005",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I agree with the Court's understanding of the high bar required to bring an action under 42 U. S. C. \u00a7 1983 for the violation of a federal statute, but I disagree with how that standard applies in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0006",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The two FNHRA provisions that respondent invokes demonstrate what it takes to satisfy this demanding standard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0007",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the rights created by a later statute `may be asserted within the remedial framework' of the earlier one."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0009",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "\u00a7 1396r(c)(1)(A)(vi). States, in turn, are obligated to \u201cinvestigate complaints of violations of requirements by nursing facilities\u201d and to take enforcement actions to correct those violations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0006-0010",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In short, \u201c[a]llowing a plaintiff to circumvent [FNHRA's] administrative remedies would be inconsistent with Congress' carefully tailored scheme.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-806",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "d9756d09297f785ff1165238e23aae0417a9acda77bcf0a380e456708297d628",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d9756d09297f-0007-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The attached opinion has been revised to refect the usual publication and citation style of the United States Reports."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
